# Gold rhyme annotation — Gilbert & Sullivan, "The Pirates of Penzance"
# (1879), the Major-General's song, first quatrain.
# Annotator: claude (draft; written from the verse text, not scanner output)

verse:
  I am the very model of a modern Major-General,
  I've information vegetable, animal, and mineral,
  I know the kings of England, and I quote the fights historical
  From Marathon to Waterloo, in order categorical

# the famous comic rhyme: Gen-er-al / an-i-mal / min-er-al.
# UNCERTAIN: "vegetable" only rhymes if you sing it the way the patter
# song forces it; left out here — add it if your ear (or Sullivan) insists.
group: General@0.9 animal@1.3 mineral@1.5

group: historical@2.11 categorical@3.6

# UNCERTAIN: "I know the kings" / "I quote the fights" — the parallel
# structure makes know~quote land as OW assonance for me. Cut if not.
group: know@2.1 quote@2.8
